summary:
  The artist links are offered for whatever stands in front of the dash,
  the station's own name included.

history:
  A title line is not always a song. "Kiss FM - The Morning Show" parses
  to the artist "Kiss FM", and a link that searches the artists of Last.fm
  for a radio station leads to a stranger of the same name. The cover
  lookup already asks TrackLogic.stationTalk before it believes such a
  line, and MusicLinks.artist asks the same question before it offers a
  link. This mutant believes every line.

target:
  package/contents/ui/MusicLinks.js

find:
      return who !== "" && TrackLogic.stationTalk(who, typeof station === "string" ? station : "") ? "" : who;

replace:
      return who;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_musiclinks.qml::test_a_station_is_not_an_artist.
  Line-neutral.
